.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KUBE-DEMO 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kube-demo
.Nd narrated demonstrations of Kubernetes on ZFS instant clones, one at a time or from a menu
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -no-pause
.Nm
.Fl -list
.Nm
.Ar demo
.Op Ar argument ...
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
With no
.Ar demo ,
.Nm
shows a menu of demonstrations on the cluster
.Xr kube-cluster 8
built, each narrated and pausing between sections.
With one, a name
.Fl -list
prints, it runs that demonstration once without pauses and exits; the web
console's Demos panel runs them that way.
.Pp
Among them: the platform and its ZFS layout; cloning a node from the
golden in milliseconds and adding or removing nodes; Cilium, Hubble,
CoreDNS, network policy, MetalLB and the Gateway API; ZFS-backed volumes,
snapshotting and restoring one, a database on one; scaling, rolling
updates, self-healing, draining, rolling a node back, replacing nodes;
eBPF from the kernel up, and a packet's path; and a Java storefront with
a database, deployed, broken, recovered and checked.
.Pp
The demonstrations change the cluster.
.Cm cleanup
removes what they made;
.Cm javaapi_destroy
removes the storefront, and asks first on a terminal.
It runs itself under
.Xr sudo 8 .
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -no-pause , Fl n
No waiting between sections, for output that is piped or captured.
.It Fl -list
Every demonstration's name.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print usage and exit 0.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev KUBE_DEMO_COUNT
How many clones the clone demonstration makes; default 1.
.It Ev KUBECONFIG
Default
.Pa /root/.kube/config .
.It Ev KLDLOAD_DEMO_YES
1:
.Cm javaapi_destroy
does not ask.
With no terminal it does not ask either.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
The demonstration's own; 1 when no control plane answers; 2 for a name
that is not a demonstration.
.Sh EXAMPLES
On a kldload desktop with no cluster, on 2026-09-30, with this release's
.Nm
first on the path:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ kube-demo frob
No Kubernetes control plane found.
# (exited 1)
.Ed
.Pp
On a cluster; not run for this page:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# kube-demo zfs_clones
# kube-demo remove_nodes 3
# kube-demo --no-pause | tee demo.log
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kube-bluegreen 8 ,
.Xr kube-cluster 8 ,
.Xr kube-demo-image 8 ,
.Xr kube-demo-publish 8 ,
.Xr kvm-demo 8
.Sh HISTORY
Before build 45 the storefront's destroy button in the web console did
nothing: with no terminal, its question read end of input as
.Dq no .
On 2026-09-30, writing this page: the clone step booted and then
destroyed any machine already called
.Ql demo-vm ,
and the help described a read-only tool that took no arguments.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
Every function named
.Ql demo_ Ns Ar name
can be run by name, including ones the list leaves out.
